  <h2>Start with the actual shopping journey</h2>
  <p>Before moving products, observe how customers use the store. Can they identify the category and price from the entrance? Are cans visible behind the items in front? Can shoppers reach snacks without moving a display? A clear section depends on more than reference count. Customers should recognise the universe, understand what they can eat or drink and find the information needed to choose.</p>
  <p>Photograph the original display and record the observation period. This gives you a reference for subsequent tests. Set a specific objective: introduce a range, simplify choice or reduce stockouts on a reference. Avoid changing pricing, location and the entire assortment at once, because it becomes difficult to understand the cause of any sales change.</p>
  <h2>Keep each product category understandable</h2>
  <p>One licence can connect several food families, but each retains its own use. A drink must read as a drink and confectionery as confectionery. Combine character recognition with clear category, format and price information. <a href="{{ path('app_products.en') }}">ULTRAPOP drinks, snacks and confectionery ranges</a> can share a corner while each family remains easy to identify.</p>
